        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualText ID="4" CompositionName="Comment">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="5" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>All the cyclical read and write commands can be issued from this Function Block.
The cyclic commands are triggered following a positive trigger. These commands are Tare Immediate, Tare Stable, Zero Immediate, Zero Stable, Pretare and Clear Tare. 
Upon successful execution of these commands, the DONE output bit will be set ON.
ERROR output bit will be set on if there is an error with the command execution.
Note: Only one cyclic command is possible at any one time.
If Net weight is required after executed a zero or tare command, insert decimal value "3" into the "WeightCmd" variable before triggering the cyclic scale command. Else, with decimal value "1" in the "WeightCmd" variable, the Function Block will return Gross Weight after the cyclic scale command. 
"DataOK" bit is set ON when the scale is in operation mode, not overloaded and not underload.</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
          <MultilingualText ID="6" CompositionName="Title">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="7" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Cyclic Weighing Data</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
        </ObjectList>
